{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410452-first-attempt-at-story-telling","id":1410452,"title":"First attempt at Story telling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-25T23:18:58-07:00","id":1410452,"title":"First attempt at Story telling","content":"so I've been obsessed with the chronicles of darkness system for a long time but this is my first attempt at creating a chronicle myself. I'm working on the Big Bad of my story and I'm having some trouble with creating balanced Bans and Banes. I'm wanting to make a rank 5 spirit of tribulation. It exists to find what a person, place, or thing lacks and tests them in a way that they either come out stronger or are destroyed by the experience. A Ban I know I want it to have is that it can't bring a test against a target that it has no chance to overcome. However it's power scales with it's target. A drug addicte will be tested in such a way that he will either overcome his addiction or over dose. A city with a poor disaster plan could find itself tested by month long flooding with no regard to how many homeless drown in the fallout. So long as the city itself could survive the test it's all fair game. I'm drawing a complete blank on a suitable Bane. I also want it to provide a Boon to anything that overcomes it's test but I'm not sure how to create a well balanced Boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/182-sciurrus","name":"sciurrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T00:18:41-07:00","id":1410460,"title":"","content":"My first thought is interference from an outside source, someone not included within the parameters of the test.<br /> As for a Boon, the test is supposed to kill you or make you stronger, perhaps an increase of a Resistance trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T07:27:09-07:00","id":1410510,"title":"","content":"If this spirit of tribulation is a being from the Shadow, it may be wise to consider its origins and/or history \u2014 remember that most spirits above Rank 3 are unlikely to be pure avatars of a descriptive concept so much as aggregated collections of related phenomena.<br /> <br /> Did it start out as a spirit of a particular person's tribulation? Maybe pieces of their corpse or the fruits of their success do unspeakable harm to it.<br /> <br /> Has it arrived at the descriptive label of &quot;spirit of tribulation&quot; by consuming spirits of disaster and despair and fortitude and faith from a separate portfolio? Maybe a devotional symbol made of a particular type of resilient material and prepared in a particular way will ward it off.<br /> <br /> Was it a disease spirit that found resonance with the increased immunity of its surviving victims? Start from the medical and occult associations with that disease and/or its cure and refine from there.<br /> <br /> Did a Master of Spirit just straight-up make the damn thing? Think about what that mage was like and what sort of Bane they might have built into such a creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}